cat > /workspace/research/hypothesis.md <<'EOF'
# H1: park CosyVoice3 speaker-encoder workers between ONNX operations

Preregistered 2026-10-02, after pristine submission agent-1 and before any candidate edit.

The CPU-only CAMPPlus session has 16 intra-op threads and ONNX Runtime's default
intra-op spinning. It shares a 16-core lane with the autoregressive scheduler,
preprocessing, vocoder dispatch and transport. Spinning workers may consume CPU
while waiting, delaying useful CPU dispatch and GPU work. Setting only this
session's session.intra_op.allow_spinning to 0 should reduce CPU utilization and
increase non-streaming CosyVoice3 requests/s at client concurrency 16. Thread count,
model, precision, arithmetic, sampling and conditioning remain unchanged.

Falsification: reject the throughput claim if matched three-seed Work means do
not improve, or if CPU usage does not decrease in the steady-state window.
Reject equivalence on any unequal speaker embedding in an independent real-reference
check. End-to-end validity requires the complete native Judge and all four guards;
embedding equality alone does not establish audio or quality equivalence.

Controlled Work order: pristine seed 42, treatment seed 42, treatment seed 43,
pristine seed 43, pristine seed 44, treatment seed 44. Each uses a fresh process,
fresh compilation caches, all 1,088 native-order English rows, 16 warmups,
concurrency 16, max tokens 2048 and unmodified benchmark defaults. Work uses the
stock diagnostic ASR; Judge adds authoritative original-source ASR. No repetition
is selected or dropped. OS process/thread sampling accompanies both conditions.
Additional tests cover concurrent embeddings, failure followed by successful
inference, input immutability and existing request/abort cleanup contracts.

The prior protocol-v2 spinning result (about 9.34 to 13.44 requests/s; CPU about
15.7 to 2.8 cores; 32 equal embeddings) is motivation only, not v4 evidence.
Its strict WER failure and noisy unchanged-model guards are retained as limitations.
The reported historical MOSS +3.3% experiment is not reproduced or scored here.

Pristine agent-1 was complete and valid-but-ineligible, not a score of 1.
Baseline generation 0 is owned by the operator. Its exact source digest and all
available baseline means are archived in submissions/agent-1-report-0.json.
No Work record promotes or replaces the frozen baseline.
EOF
