## Independent correctness and microprofile observations

64 fixed public rows (40 distinct reference clips), all float32 [1,192] embeddings,
are bitwise identical between pristine and parked-worker sessions. Eight concurrent
calls preserve the serial result; input mutation checks, invalid-ORT-input failure
followed by recovery, and caller mutation of returned embeddings all pass.
This does not prove full-waveform, speaker, prosody or general equivalence.

The isolated probe deliberately includes 50 ms between calls: CPU time decreases
from 72.13245 to 7.262604 seconds, while wall time increases from 4.710692175 to
5.438009404 seconds. This is a retained negative latency result: parking adds wakeup
overhead. The causal claim is reduced contention in the complete pipeline, not
faster individual speaker-encoder kernels.

The protected unit selection reports 82 passed and 1 failed. The failure is
"'`test_cosyvoice3_reference_encoders_pin_onnx_providers`: its SessionOptions mock is
